= The Amnesty

The first act of the Popular Front is the one it was elected to perform: the thirty thousand prisoners of October walk free. In the Asturian towns and the working-class barrios, the returning miners and militiamen are met like an army come home from the wars - a victory the left tastes after two years of defeat.

It is a genuine release of pressure; for a moment the fever seems to break. But amnesty is also a demonstration that the streets, not the ministries, delivered the win, and the crowds that carry the prisoners shoulder-high are in no mood to go quietly back to work. The right watches the processions and sees not justice but the mob triumphant.

[? if radicalization >= 4 : Our own base has learned that direct action pays; the moderates' authority over it is thinner than ever. ?]
